  "reason": "The faulty capability was customers.lookup@1 (src/handlers/customers.lookup.mjs). It read the static legacy CRM export (src/legacy/crm.mjs), while customers.register@1 writes to the application store (src/store.mjs). That store is the system of record for urn:example:customers:customer and is seeded from the same export at start-up, so newly registered customers could never be read back. Lookup now reads from the store via getCustomer and returns the same five contract fields. It still fails with NOT_FOUND for unknown IDs. Only the lookup handler changed; no contract or test was modified. The proposal passed all verification checks: unchanged contract digest, conforming outputs, only declared failures, and unchanged answers on existing state for customers.lookup@1 and billing.contact@1. The declared customer-readable and registered-event verification of customers.register@1 now confirms. One residual point: lookup returns a fresh object rather than the store's stored reference, so callers cannot mutate store state through the result.",
